<title>UK: TABLE - Securicor H1 profits hit by excepts.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Securicor H1 profits hit by excepts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  5.5		  vs   5.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   0.39		 vs   0.354</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excepts	56.1		  vs  53.8</p>
<p> Pretax			19.1		  vs  47.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   673.2		  vs 612.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 45.0 and 55.0 million stg.</p>
<p>Earnings per share is before exceptional items and discontinued operations. Exceptional items and discountinued operations amounted to 28.9 million stg versus 3.9 million stg the previous year. This includes the exceptional write-off, announced in March, of 18 million stg in Securicor Cellular Services related to amortization costs applied to subscriber acquisition costs within SCS.</p>
<p>Full company name - Securicor Group Plc.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
